# behavior: a module-scoped `yield` fixture is set up at its first use, just before the first test that needs it, and torn down after the file's last test, as 0.5.1 does (#3149).
# cli-commands:
#   test tests/test_lazy.incn --nocapture
# expect-stdout:
#
#   running 1 test
#   early test
#   test_lazy.incn::test_early PASSED
#   late setup
#   uses late
#   test_lazy.incn::test_uses_late PASSED
#   after
#   late teardown
#   test incan_case_group ... ok
#
#   test result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in <duration>
#
#   test_lazy.incn::test_after PASSED

